# Project: Hazel's portfolio site

A personal site with two sections reachable from the menu: Portfolio (landing page,
case studies, CV, skills, contact) and Cumpleaños (built later). The owner, Hazel,
edits all content herself through a CMS at /admin, so the code must never be the
place where content lives.

## Stack
- Framework: Astro, static output.
- Hosting: Cloudflare Pages. Build command `npm run build`, output folder `dist/`.
- CMS: Sveltia CMS served at `/admin` (Decap-compatible `public/admin/config.yml`),
  GitHub backend, login handled by a separate Cloudflare Worker (base_url in config).
- Styling: CSS custom properties for every design token. No hardcoded colors,
  font families, radii, or shadows inside components.

## Folder map
- `src/content/projects/`   one Markdown file per case study
- `src/content/settings/profile.json`   name, bio, CV entries, skills, social links
- `src/content/settings/theme.json`     design choices Hazel can change
- `src/assets/uploads/`     images uploaded through the CMS (kept under src/ so
                            Astro can optimize them)
- `src/components/`         one component per section
- `src/styles/tokens.css`   all design tokens and the named token sets
- `public/admin/`           CMS entry point (index.html + config.yml)

## Golden rules
1. No hardcoded content. Every text, image, link, and list on the page comes from
   `src/content/`. If a component needs new content, add a field; never inline copy.
2. Every content field exists in TWO places and they must match: the Astro content
   collection schema AND `public/admin/config.yml`. When you add, rename, or remove
   a field, update both in the same change and tell me you did.
3. `theme.json` only stores choices from predefined options (for example
   accent: pink | yellow | periwinkle). It never stores raw hex values. Each option
   maps to a token set defined in `src/styles/tokens.css`.
4. Section order and visibility come from the `sections` list in `theme.json`.
   The page renders sections in that order and skips hidden ones.
5. Images go through Astro's image pipeline (the `image()` schema helper and
   `<Image />`). Verify that the path format the CMS writes for uploads resolves
   correctly with that helper, and test it with a real upload.
6. Mobile-first, responsive, WCAG AA contrast, respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
7. Do not add dependencies without asking me first. Pin exact versions.
8. Work in small steps. After each step, run `npm run build` and fix any error
   before continuing. Summarize what changed and which files you touched.

## Design direction
Editorial structure (generous whitespace, strong grid, thin dividers, image-led
project cards) with playful accents used sparingly (thick outlines, hard offset
shadows with no blur, a few sticker-like shapes, bold accent color in the hero).
Use the UI UX Pro Max skill for design-system decisions.

## Out of scope for you (the human does these)
- Creating the GitHub repo, OAuth app, and adding Hazel as a collaborator.
- Anything in the Cloudflare dashboard, and deploying or configuring the auth Worker.
- Secrets: never write client secrets, tokens, or keys into any file in this repo.
  If a step needs one, stop and tell me where it should be configured.

## Feature specs
- Every feature has a spec in `docs/specs/`. Before implementing a feature, read
  its spec AND `docs/specs/00-roadmap.md`.
- Follow the spec's PROCESS steps in order and stop for review after each one.
- When a step is approved, tick its checkbox in `00-roadmap.md`.
- If a spec conflicts with these rules or with the existing template, stop and
  tell me instead of guessing.
